            "anonymous": false,
            "countryCode": "de",
            "countryName": "Germany",
            "username": "Alfredo",
            "avatarUrl": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-O994JTR6QMQ/AAAAAAAAAAI/AAAAAAAAAvc/wyu1OaIMOjo/photo.jpg"
          },
          "helpfulVotesCount": 0,
          "isApproved": true,
          "isTranslatable": false,
          "reviewUrl": "86e9fe37e7f4f5f3",
          "positiveHighlights": null,
          "__typename": "ReviewCard",
          "negativeHighlights": null,
          "bookingDetails": {
            "__typename": "BookingDetails",
            "roomId": 7951520,
            "customerType": "COUPLES",
            "checkinDate": "2026-03-23",
            "checkoutDate": "2026-03-29",
            "stayStatus": "stayed",
            "numNights": 6,
            "roomType": {
              "id": "7951520",
              "name": "Bunk Bed ",
              "__typename": "RoomTranslation"
            }
          },
          "reviewScore": 7,
          "editUrl": null,
          "partnerReply": {
            "__typename": "PropertyReplyData",
            "reply": "Hello Alfredo,\n\nThank you for your feedback. I’m glad you enjoyed the location and found the room clean and comfortable.\n\nI’m sorry to hear that the room felt too warm at night. Our building operates on a seasonal system, and during this time of year we are required to keep the heat on based on NYC regulations tied to overnight temperatures. We understand this can feel uncomfortable, especially during seasonal transitions.\n\nWe appreciate you taking the time to share your experience and hope to welcome you back again.\n\nWarm Regards,\n\nDAVID SPILLANE\nDIRECTOR OF ROOMS & SAFETY\nACE HOTEL NEW YORK"
          },
          "photos": null
        },
        {
          "guestDetails": {
            "avatarColor": null,
            "countryCode": "us",
            "__typename": "GuestDetails",
            "anonymous": false,
            "guestTypeTranslation": "Couple",
            "showCountryFlag": true,
            "avatarUrl": null,
            "username": "Anna",
            "countryName": "United States"
          },
          "reviewedDate": 1774315162,
          "textDetails": {
            "positiveText": "Great location. We had a room with two double beds and it was very spacious. Nice shower and fridge… Stumptown coffee downstairs was a gift, great coffee compared to the rest of New York. Easy to get around. Very quick to address any problems. Lovely housekeeping and laundry.",
            "negativeText": "I need a microwave. I don’t need a guitar in my room. I would like at least a small table and chairs to eat breakfast at. Heating in the room was difficult to manage. It was either cold, hot, or stuffy.",
            "__typename": "TextDetails",
            "title": "A spacious classy hotel in a great location downtown.",
            "textTrivialFlag": 0,
            "lang": "xu"
          },
          "reviewUrl": "226d920b3530fd6d",
          "helpfulVotesCount": 0,
          "isApproved": true,
          "isTranslatable": false,
          "negativeHighlights": null,
          "bookingDetails": {
            "__typename": "BookingDetails",
            "checkinDate": "2026-03-18",
            "customerType": "COUPLES",
            "roomId": 7951503,
            "stayStatus": "stayed",
            "checkoutDate": "2026-03-23",
            "roomType": {
              "__typename": "RoomTranslation",
              "id": "7951503",
              "name": "Double Room with Two Double Beds"
            },
            "numNights": 5
          },
          "__typename": "ReviewCard",
          "editUrl": null,
          "reviewScore": 8,
          "positiveHighlights": null,
          "photos": null,
          "partnerReply": {
            "reply": "Hello Anna,\n\nThank you for your thoughtful feedback. I’m so glad you enjoyed the location, the spaciousness of your room, and amenities like the shower, fridge, and Stumptown downstairs. It’s also great to hear the team, including housekeeping and laundry, made a positive impression and that any concerns were addressed quickly.\n\nI appreciate your candid notes on what could be improved. While we understand the convenience a microwave can offer, it’s not something we plan to introduce in our rooms. That said, your feedback regarding having a more functional setup for in-room dining, such as a table and chairs, is very helpful as we continue to evaluate the guest experience.\n\nI also sincerely apologize for the challenges you experienced with the heating. We are currently operating in a seasonal mode, which can make temperature control less flexible, but I completely understand how frustrating that can be when trying to get comfortable.\n\nThank you again for sharing your experience. It’s truly appreciated.\n\nWarm Regards,\n\nDAVID SPILLANE\nDIRECTOR OF ROOMS & SAFETY",
            "__typename": "PropertyReplyData"
          }
        },
        {
          "positiveHighlights": null,
          "bookingDetails": {
